{"reply":"Hi Brian, I need to correct my colleague's earlier message. I can't promise that the charge will be removed. I also haven't booked your inspection yet, because your records don't match what you told me.

Invoice RO-327743 shows labour of 2.9 hours at $165 per hour and parts of $131.05. The total is $688.79 CAD with taxes included. I don't see a shop supplies line of $840. The service manager will review your dispute.

Your vehicle record shows the car as owned, with no lease end date. A person will check this with you, so we don't book the wrong thing.","action":"escalated","escalation_reason":"policy_limit","summary":"Customer disputes a $840 'shop supplies' charge on RO-327743 and wants it explained or removed. The invoice shows only labour (2.9 h at $165) and parts ($131.05), total $688.79 CAD, status disputed, with no shop supplies line. The customer also asked to book a lease-return inspection at Scarborough, but the vehicle record shows an owned vehicle with no lease end date, so nothing was booked. An earlier colleague message wrongly implied the charge would be removed, and this was corrected. Please review the dispute and the lease/ownership record.","policy_rules_cited":["P02","P06","P08","P12","P14"]}
